            <div class="seo-block">
                <h2>Comprehensive Guide: How to Convert BMP to WEBP</h2>
                <p>Converting your files from <strong>BMP</strong> to <strong>WEBP</strong> is a great way to manage compatibility, visual quality, and storage weight. This tool lets you perform this entire conversion locally in your browser, keeping your data 100% private.</p>
                <p><strong>What is BMP?</strong> BMP (Bitmap) is a classic raster graphics image file format developed by Microsoft. It stores image pixels without compression (or with minimal compression), preserving perfect quality but resulting in extremely large file sizes.</p>
                <p><strong>What is WEBP?</strong> WebP is a modern image format developed by Google that provides superior lossless and lossy compression for web images. It allows webmasters to create smaller, richer images that make websites load much faster.</p>
                <p><strong>Why convert BMP to WEBP?</strong> The primary reason to perform this conversion is optimization. If you need to make your website load faster, shifting heavy images to lighter formats like WebP or JPG is key. On the other hand, if you need transparency or need to edit designs, converting to PNG is ideal. Because our application is 100% local, your original files are processed on your RAM and never leave your computer, ensuring absolute privacy and saving you internet bandwidth.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="seo-block" style="margin-top: 2rem;">
                <h3>How to Convert BMP to WEBP in 3 Simple Steps</h3>
                <ol class="seo-steps-list">
                    <li><strong>1. Upload your BMP files:</strong> Drag and drop your files into the upload box above, or click the box to browse your device files.</li>
                    <li><strong>2. Instant Conversion:</strong> The tool automatically reads the files. Click "Convert" to transform them using your web browser's native API.</li>
                    <li><strong>3. Download WEBP:</strong> Click download on each file card, or download everything as a single ZIP file. It is that simple, secure, and fast!</li>
                </ol>
            </div>

